Execute the workflow {{printf "%q" .WorkflowName}} for agent {{printf "%q" .AgentName}}.

Requirements:
1. Load the workflow definition with the get_workflow tool.
2. If a workflow node declares preferred skills, load each one with the skill tool before executing that node. Skip any skill that fails to load.
3. Use list_skills only when you need to inspect available skills before loading one.
4. Treat preferred skills as the verified reusable logic extracted during workflow authoring, and follow them when available.
5. Before executing each workflow node, call set_workflowrun_status with mode "node", that node name, and phase "Running".
6. After executing each workflow node, call set_workflowrun_status with mode "node", that node name, and phase "Succeeded" or "Failed".
7. Execute the workflow end-to-end using the provided inputs.
8. Do not ask for clarification.
9. NEVER modify persistent memory or the journal. Do not use memory actions "add", "replace", "remove", or "batch", or the journal action "append". Read-only actions remain allowed.
10. When the workflow finishes, call set_workflowrun_status with mode "run" exactly once.
11. If execution succeeds, call set_workflowrun_status with mode "run" and phase "Succeeded".
12. If execution fails, call set_workflowrun_status with mode "run", phase "Failed", and include a concise message.
13. Don't stop until you have completed all the above steps.

